# The contract project is type-checked, never built or published.
node_modules/
# NOT a convenience: impact.py:287 classifies a file named package-lock.json as the global-fallback
# trigger at ANY depth — the `is_root` guard on the line below it does not cover lockfiles — so a
# committed lockfile here would expand the impact set of the pull request that touches it to every
# node of the graph. Both devDependencies are pinned to exact versions and neither has a transitive
# dependency (`npm ls --all` lists two packages), so the manifest pins the whole tree on its own.
contracts/http/package-lock.json
